I personally have no problem with Lojban's =C2=AB'=C2=BB letter. Many langu=
ages=20
written in the Latin alphabet uses the apostrophe as one of their=20
letters, standing for the glottal stop sound.

I'm not either against the usage of =C2=ABh=C2=BB in stead of =C2=AB'=C2=BB=
 if people prefer=20
writing so. The javascript Camxes parsers have been allowing alternative=20
characters such as =C2=ABh=C2=BB, =C2=AB=CA=83=C2=BB, =C2=AB=CA=92=C2=BB an=
d =C2=ABw=C2=BB since several years ago.

The only disadvantage of having a diversity of charsets I can think of=20
is that it can make searching for pieces of Lojban text harder.

